+# Combo variant of b9e38dc0 (index 4)
+# combo_spec: D3/0+D14/0
+# Name: 周期性颜色+开口宽度射线
+
+"""
+Design analysis for the combo variant
+=====================================
+
+a) Concrete behavior and trace:
+   Start from the original chamber-fill task, but fuse two trajectory changes at
+   the same place in the pipeline: the outgoing region is no longer a wedge, and
+   it is no longer monochrome.
+   Example with upward radiation:
+   - Original: the solver floods the interior, then lets fill escape between two
+     boundary rays; every reachable outside cell becomes the seed color.
+   - D14 part: close the mouth during the interior flood, measure the mouth cells
+     between the two endpoints, then extrude those exact cells straight upward to
+     the border. This makes a constant-width strip whose width equals the opening.
+   - D3 part: after obstacle shadows are resolved, recolor only that strip by
+     depth bands using an AABB cycle built from seed color and wall color:
+       depth 0-1 -> seed, 2-3 -> wall, 4-5 -> seed, ...
+   Difference from the original: the output now shows a wide striped bar instead
+   of a widening solid-color fan.
+
+b) Complexity calibration:
+   The combo still uses only the already-visible semantic colors: wall and seed.
+   The new free variables stay limited and repeated:
+   - opening width varies with wall geometry, typically 4-6 cells
+   - stripe pattern is fixed globally as AABB, not instance-specific
+   This keeps the rule inferable while ensuring the fusion is visually distinct.
+
+c) Hidden-assumption audit:
+   The original `barrier` logic assumed two 1-pixel rays were enough to define
+   the outside region. That fails once the radiation must be an equal-width band,
+   so the combo replaces ray barriers with explicit mouth detection plus strip
+   extrusion. The original `out[filled_mask] = fill` also assumed one paint color
+   for all reachable cells; now coloring must happen after shadow trimming so the
+   surviving strip cells can be assigned by depth band. The shadow pass itself
+   still works because it depends on a boolean painted mask, not on final colors.
+   New solver assumptions are:
+   - the chosen wall component has two usable degree-1 endpoints
+   - the mouth between them is a straight row/column segment orthogonal to the
+     radiation direction
+   - the mouth cells are left empty by the generator
+   The generator below enforces all three.
+
+d) Placement legality:
+   The wall builder is unchanged structurally, so wall pixels stay 8-connected,
+   in-bounds, and within the original size ranges. The anchor logic now reserves
+   at least six visible depths from the mouth to the border so the periodic band
+   can display both colors multiple times. Obstacles are still placed only on
+   background cells and kept away from the wall, which prevents overlap with the
+   wall and seed while preserving legal shadow behavior.
+
+e) Visual observability:
+   Across a few examples, a human can read the rule from geometry and repeated
+   color structure alone: the mouth visibly determines strip width, and the strip
+   itself alternates between the wall color and seed color in repeated parallel
+   bands. No inference relies on color ids or hidden ordering.
+
+f) Visual neatness:
+   The combo deliberately keeps layering simple:
+   - interior chamber: solid seed color
+   - outgoing region: one clean constant-width strip
+   - strip coloring: depth-parallel bands only
+   Obstacles remain sparse singleton interruptions, so the scene stays legible.
+
+g) Change inferability:
+   Only two trajectory colors participate in the pattern, and both are already
+   anchored to meaningful objects in the input. Because the repeated wall-colored
+   bands appear only in the emitted strip and not elsewhere, the mapping
+   "wall+seed alternate on the strip" is recoverable from 2-3 examples.
+"""
+
+import random
+import sys
+
+import numpy as np
+from scipy.ndimage import distance_transform_cdt
+
+sys.path.append("/home/lixinyu/snap/new/solvers")
+from arc_utils import components_mask, get_bg, neighbors4, neighbors8
+
+
+# -- Configuration constants --------------------------------------------------
+# Canvas size bounds
+GRID_H_VERT = (11, 18)
+GRID_H_HORIZ = (8, 18)
+GRID_W = (15, 19)
+
+# Wall geometry
+WALL_PIXELS_MIN = 17
+WALL_PIXELS_MAX = 25
+DEPTH_VERT = (5, 10)
+DEPTH_HORIZ = (6, 8)
+GAP_VERT = (6, 7)
+GAP_HORIZ = (5, 7)
+TIP_12_PROB = 0.5
+
+# Placement margins
+OPEN_END_MARGIN = 3
+PATTERN_REPEAT_DEPTH = 5  # need depths 0..5 to expose seed/seed/wall/wall/seed/seed
+
+# Fill seed
+SEED_SIZE_WEIGHTS = [1, 1, 1, 1, 2, 2, 3, 4, 5, 6]
+SEED_DEPTH_LOOKBACK = 3
+
+# Obstacles
+MAX_OBSTACLES = 5
+OBSTACLE_IN_FILL_PROB = 0.65
+OBSTACLE_MIN_SEP = 2
